-### [Histogram Spectra for LOD Selection](11687-histogram-spectra-for-lod-selection.md)
-Histogram Spectra for LOD Selection (HSPE) is a metadata-driven technique for selecting Level of Detail (LOD) in multivariate, time-varying volume rendering. It solves the problem of interactive LOD selection for large, out-of-core volumes by precomputing statistical sensitivity metrics, allowing error estimation without accessing the raw volume data. Unlike direct RMS error computation which requires reading the entire dataset, HSPE uses compact histogram spectra to pose LOD selection as an integer programming problem, maximizing quality within a working set size constraint. See [Histogram Spectra for LOD Selection](11687-histogram-spectra-for-lod-selection.md).
